 "size_basis": "Not dimensioned in CAPR 39-1. The hand is the guidance figure's glove (one drawing, 130 x 126 px as the coat figures show it under a 144.6 px cuff; the figure used for this sheet has a 144.6 px cuff) scaled to this sheet's cuff, each hand by its own cuff: right hand 48.6 px/in, cuff 2.97 in, left hand 49.0 px/in, cuff 2.95 in; at the figures' belt scale (46.4 px/in) the same glove would be 2.80 in wide. The top of the glove lies on the sheet's own cuff line (the outline's lower sleeve edge) and goes under the sleeve, so the cuff covers the wrist. Box: the sheet's box with 1.85 in more below (the fingers hang past the sheet's lower edge); the sheet's box lies at 0,0 inside it (landmark sheet_box).",
 "provenance": "in-house vector. Measured on the Class A guard and flag bearer figures and the Class B long sleeve figure of \"CAP Honor Guard Uniform Guidance\" (page 4, 3672 x 4752 px): the six gloves' flat fill (249 grey) isolated as masks (11,381 to 11,663 px each on the coat figures, 130 x 126 px), their stroke thinned to centre lines (Zhang-Suen) and traced into branches (outline with the four fingertip lobes, three finger divisions, the thumb's loop, crease and side line). Cuff frame: the sleeve's lower edge line fitted per glove (angle 6.7 to 6.9 degrees), the outer corner where it meets the sleeve's outer edge line. The four coat gloves coincide in that frame, one mirrored for the other, to 0.38 to 0.68 px mean and 1.9 px at the most; averaged branch by branch (spread at most 1.2 px). The Class B long figure's two gloves match the same drawing to 0.65 px mean after a shift of (-5.3, +25.6) px (L: -5.7, +28.2; R: -5.0, +23.0): there the sleeve covers 25.6 px less of the hand. Cuff widths on the figures (corner to the coat or trousers edge, along the cuff line): Class A guard and flag bearer, four gloves: cuff widths 144.9, 144.3, 144.3, 145.0 px; Class B long sleeve, two gloves: cuff widths 126.0 and 129.9 px; the glove sits (-5.7, 28.2) and (-5.0, 23.0) px from the coat figure's in the cuff frame. The hand's inner edge is behind the coat or the trousers in every figure and is drawn here as a straight edge 0.05 in beyond the sheet's own body edge, so the body hides it; the sleeve's outline is not covered (mask stroke 0.053 in). On this sheet the cuff's corner and edge lines come from the outline path's vertices L: outer 37,36, cuff 34,33, stop 32,31; R: outer 22,23, cuff 24,25, stop 26,27 (indices into the silhouette path; the outer corner of each sleeve, inches: right O (1.03, 28.89), cuff rises 4.8 deg toward the body; left O (23.35, 28.89), cuff rises 4.8 deg toward the body).",
